unit: dm-decision-extractor-move
commits: 8f19c1bc4 (the move)
what: sovereign-api/src/middleware/decision_extractor.rs (443) and
  sovereign-tools/src/notes/response_mine.rs (454) moved to corpus-engine-notes
  (DT `workspace` cluster, dest corpus-engine-notes). decision_extractor.rs
  repointed: `corpus_engine_notes::` -> `crate::`, `sovereign_tools::notes::
  response_mine` -> `crate::response_mine`, `super::{Middleware, …}` ->
  `sovereign_contracts::middleware::{…}`, `crate::openai_types::` ->
  `oicp_types::openai_types::`, `sovereign_core::middleware::notes_db_path` ->
  `sovereign_contracts::middleware::notes_db_path` (defined at
  sovereign-contracts/src/middleware.rs:242, so repointed not moved). Shims keep
  old paths live: `pub use corpus_engine_notes::decision_extractor;` in
  sovereign-api/src/middleware/mod.rs, `pub use corpus_engine_notes::response_mine;`
  in sovereign-tools/src/notes/mod.rs (audit_recover.rs:71 still compiles).
  corpus-engine-notes gains sovereign-contracts + oicp-types + async-trait and a
  `test-fixtures` dev-dep; the middleware-directory guard's walk floor drops
  `scanned >= 3` -> `>= 2`; DT [[module]] rows re-keyed to corpus-engine-notes/src/.
  Premise correction (PROMPT §6, ralph/DECISIONS.md): the row predated
  REVIEW-build-middleware-seam (7ea3d6aae), so its line numbers were stale, and
  naming sovereign-contracts from corpus-engine-notes grows that leaf's fan-in
  31 -> 32 — quality/baselines/fan_in.tsv hand-raised ONE line with a
  SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md §10.1ac ledger (--update-baseline not run).
checks: CLEAN exit=0; LINT exit=0 (15 crates, errors: 0); LAYER exit=0
